(PRC-27 — `Create symbolic link from '<target>' to "<linkpath>".` performs
 symlink(2): the SECOND path is the link that gets created, and it points
 at the FIRST. The probe pins the direction two ways — it reads a file
 through the link, and it makes a link to a target that does not exist and
 finds the link unresolvable rather than the statement failing.
 Also covers: PRC-28 (the error flag is set on failure — the second
 identical symlink fails with EEXIST).
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-27.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the link resolves
   payload
   a link to a missing target does not resolve
   creating the same link twice set the error flag
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
open a file for writing called scribe at "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_real.txt".
Write "payload" to scribe.
Close scribe.
Create symbolic link from "scratch_real.txt" to "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_link".
On error print "the symbolic link failed".
If "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_link" is available then, print "the link resolves".
a buffer called 'read through the link' is 32 bytes in size.
open a file for reading called reader at "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_link".
Read from reader into 'read through the link'.
Close reader.
print 'read through the link'.
Create symbolic link from "scratch_nothing" to "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_dangling".
If "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_dangling" is not available then, print "a link to a missing target does not resolve".
Create symbolic link from "scratch_nothing" to "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_dangling".
On error print "creating the same link twice set the error flag".
Delete the file "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_link".
Delete the file "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_dangling".
Delete the file "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_real.txt".
